Third-party origins and credits
===============================

The licenses in LICENSE apply only to the original work of Antony Burrows.
The designs below are derived from, or contain parts of, other people's
work. Those parts remain the property of their authors and are NOT
relicensed by this repository. They are shared here, with credit, as a
non-commercial hobby archive.

John Monahan, S100Computers.com (http://www.s100computers.com)
  80386-CPU/          Mostly John Monahan's "S-100 80386 CPU Board" V3;
                      small V3.1 changes by Antony Burrows. Full credit to him.
  Z80-CPU/            All revisions descend from his S-100 Z80 CPU Board V2
                      KiCad files.
  SRAM-8MB/rev1/      Bus interface logic follows his S-100 16MB SRAM board.
  x86-Memory-Adapter/ The P5/P6 interface and starting files come from his
                      80386 SRAM board (V6).
  SX6-MEM/            Daughterboard header signal names follow his 80386
                      SRAM daughterboard.

Andrew Lynch and the N8VEM project
  Z80-FPGA-SBC/       The schematic started from the N8VEM SBC V2.
  Flash-UART/         The UART section follows the N8VEM ECB SBC V2.
  Backplane-18-Slot/  Rev 1.0 started from the N8VEM S-100 backplane (V02).
  (various)           KiCad symbols and footprints from the N8VEM KiCad
                      libraries, including the S-100 edge connector.

Godbout Electronics / CompuPro
  Backplane-18-Slot/, Bus-Terminator/
                      The active bus termination circuit follows the
                      CompuPro (Godbout) S-100 Active Terminator.

Not included: original third-party KiCad projects, manuals, datasheets and
software (for example S100Computers monitor and PIC/RTC programs) that were
kept alongside these projects for reference.
